#!/bin/sh
# The deb stand-in for NSIS_HOOK_PREUNINSTALL — PLAN-0009 phase 4,
# prescription 1.
#
# On Windows that hook runs the app's own binary before anything is
# deleted, to take back the one Path entry the app recorded writing.
# On Linux there is no such entry to take back: PLAN-0009 phase 3
# prescription 3 made the PATH step a report rather than a write, so
# the app never edits a shell startup file and never records one.
# This script states that absence rather than leaving it implied,
# exactly as removal.rs does for the same case, and does nothing.
#
# dpkg calls this with remove, upgrade, deconfigure or failed-upgrade
# in $1. Every case exits 0: a removal must never be stopped here.
exit 0
